## Best Practices

1. **Layer sounds** - Combine tone and noise for realistic drums
2. **Use pitch envelopes** - Essential for kicks and toms
3. **Short envelopes** - Keep drums punchy
4. **Filter noise** - Shape noise for different drum types
5. **Velocity maps** - Map velocity to envelope and filter

## Common Drum Tuning

| Drum Type | Fundamental | Envelope Decay | Noise Level |
|-----------|------------|----------------|-------------|
| Kick      | 40-80 Hz   | 100-500ms      | Low (0-20%) |
| Snare     | 150-250 Hz | 100-300ms      | High (50-80%) |
| Hi-Hat    | N/A        | 50-300ms       | 100% |
| Tom       | 80-200 Hz  | 200-400ms      | Low (0-30%) |
| Clap      | N/A        | 100-200ms      | High (80-100%) |
